 long form names one specific disease (CHRPE) with no further categorization, so the full phrase is annotated as a Specific Disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1: Specific Disease; What to Annotate 6: Synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":395,\"end\":400,\"text\":\"CHRPE\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"'CHRPE' is the abbreviation for congenital hypertrophy of the retinal pigment epithelium and is annotated as a separate mention from the long form.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 6: Synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":458,\"end\":463,\"text\":\"CHRPE\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Duplicate mention of the disease CHRPE in the same sentence as the object of 'expressing'; all disease mentions, including duplicates, are annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 4: Duplicate mentions\"},{\"start\":680,\"end\":685,\"text\":\"CHRPE\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Duplicate mention of the disease CHRPE as the subject of 'extent of'; duplicates within the same abstract are annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 4: Duplicate mentions\"},{\"start\":773,\"end\":778,\"text\":\"CHRPE\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Duplicate mention of the disease CHRPE at the start of a sentence referring to lesions; all disease mentions are annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 4: Duplicate mentions\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3913, "output_tokens": 8925, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 7990}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}